# ==============================================================================
# 24-Hour Unattended AI Worker Daemon - Environment Configuration
# Put this file in the SAME directory as worker.sh (.worker.env)
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Operating System Configuration (macOS / Ubuntu / Linux)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python 3.9+ runs the daemon, queue operations, CLI adapters, and JSON status handling.
# Override when python3 is not on PATH (for example, a virtual environment).
PYTHON_BIN="${PYTHON_BIN:-python3}"

# Options:
#   - "auto"   : Automatically detect the current OS (default)
#   - "mac"    : Report macOS
#   - "ubuntu" : Report Ubuntu Linux
#   - "linux"  : Report generic Linux
# Task timeout and process-group handling are shared across supported platforms in worker_runtime.py.
OS_TYPE="${OS_TYPE:-auto}"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Worker Identity & Parallelization
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unique identifier for this worker instance (default: "default")
# When running multiple workers in parallel worktrees, set different IDs:
# e.g., "worker-1", "worker-2", etc.
WORKER_ID="${WORKER_ID:-default}"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Model & AI CLI Configuration
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supported CLI: "codex" (OpenAI Codex CLI) or "agy" (Google Antigravity CLI)
# Active low-cost Codex example. To switch providers, change only this section.
AI_CLI="${AI_CLI:-codex}"

# Model identifiers are opaque strings owned by the selected provider.
# Changing model does not change provider; set effort to a value that model supports.
AI_MODEL="${AI_MODEL:-gpt-6-luna}"

# Reasoning effort level: none | low | medium | high | xhigh | max
AI_EFFORT="${AI_EFFORT:-none}"

# Optional ordered failover registry (first available agent is tried first).
# A switch happens only after a failed CLI call whose output clearly identifies
# quota/rate-limit exhaustion; ordinary errors and timeouts do not trigger it.
# On total exhaustion, the current task stays queued and the daemon waits.
# Reset the exhausted-agent state after quota recovery; the daemon resumes without restart.
# Explicit RUN_ONCE=1 tests exit instead of waiting.
# Remove .worker-agent-state.<WORKER_ID>.json after quota resets to re-enable agents.
# AI_AGENTS_JSON='[{"id":"codex-main","provider":"codex","command":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","effort":"none"},{"id":"agy-backup","provider":"agy","command":"agy","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-low","effort":"low","agy_mode":"accept-edits"}]'
# Registry overrides AI_CLI when present; ordering controls quota-only failover.
# Each profile: id, provider (codex|agy|generic), command (one executable),
# model, effort, agy_mode, args (literal argv array), env (string map).
# Missing model/effort/agy_mode inherit AI_MODEL/AI_EFFORT/AGY_MODE.
# Native CLI policy (CODEX_* / USE_SANDBOX) and time/budget limits remain shared.
# Unknown fields and invalid value types fail before a task is claimed.
# args are passed without shell expansion. env overrides inherited process values.
# Keep credentials in the launch environment; do not put secrets in args or JSON.
# A different HTTP API connects through a generic executable wrapper, for example:
# AI_AGENTS_JSON='[{"id":"api","provider":"generic","command":"python3","args":["/absolute/path/api_worker.py"],"model":"vendor/model","effort":"medium","env":{"API_BASE_URL":"https://api.example/v1"}}]'
# Generic wrapper protocol:
#   argv: configured args followed by the complete task prompt (one argument).
#   Environment: NIGHTSHIFT_MODEL, NIGHTSHIFT_EFFORT, NIGHTSHIFT_PROMPT_FILE,
#     NIGHTSHIFT_RESULT_FILE, NIGHTSHIFT_TASK_ID; PORT and TEST_PORT are also set.
#   Read the prompt from argv or UTF-8 PROMPT_FILE; run your API/tool loop.
#   Write the final plain-text outcome to NIGHTSHIFT_RESULT_FILE (UTF-8).
#   stdout/stderr are diagnostic logs, never the final result when the file exists.
#   Exit 0 with a nonempty result for a completed or explicitly blocked task;
#     use [BLOCKED], [SCOPE_BLOCKED], [NEED_GUIDANCE], or [NEED_DECOMPOSITION].
#   Exit nonzero on transport/provider failures; quota errors may trigger failover.
#   The host stages only TARGET paths and commits; wrappers should leave Git writes
#     to the host. Generic [CLOSEOUT_REQUIRED] is unsupported and fails closed.
#   Generic adapters have invocation timeouts; tool-action counting is their own
#     responsibility (MAX_STEPS is provided as the assigned budget).
# Optional state location override (default: .worker-agent-state.<WORKER_ID>.json).
# AI_AGENT_STATE_FILE=".worker-agent-state.default.json"

# Codex execution policy:
#   - CODEX_SANDBOX: read-only | workspace-write | danger-full-access
#   - CODEX_APPROVAL_MODE: auto (recommended unattended mode) | prompt | bypass (unsafe)
#     In auto mode Codex edits in workspace-write; the Python worker stages declared TARGET paths and commits.
#     bypass grants unrestricted host access and should only be used with external isolation.
#     CODEX_SANDBOX is used with prompt mode; auto uses Codex's workspace-write sandbox.
#   - CODEX_EPHEMERAL: 1 avoids persisting a session for each queue task
CODEX_SANDBOX="${CODEX_SANDBOX:-workspace-write}"
CODEX_APPROVAL_MODE="${CODEX_APPROVAL_MODE:-auto}"
CODEX_EPHEMERAL="${CODEX_EPHEMERAL:-1}"

# Antigravity example: AI_CLI=agy, AI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash-low,
# AI_EFFORT=low, AGY_MODE=accept-edits
# Antigravity Execution Mode:
#   - "accept-edits" : Automatically approve file edits (Recommended for unattended runs)
#   - "auto"         : Full auto approval (requires supported account tier)
#   - "plan"         : Planning only mode
AGY_MODE="${AGY_MODE:-accept-edits}"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Timeout & Polling Controls
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maximum timeout per task in seconds (default: 1800 = 30 minutes)
TASK_TIMEOUT="${TASK_TIMEOUT:-1800}"

# Dynamic Step Budget Formula: TASK_MAX_STEPS = STEP_BASE + (TARGET_FILES * STEP_PER_FILE)
# Scales automatically with the number of target files (no cap on file count).
STEP_BASE="${STEP_BASE:-12}"
STEP_PER_FILE="${STEP_PER_FILE:-5}"

# Shared Worker reliability score (1-5); new workers start at 5.
# Runtime lowers it for repeated same-task timeouts/action-budget exhaustion.
# Planner records accept/reject/no-fault feedback with an evidence pointer.
WORKER_SCORE_FILE="${WORKER_SCORE_FILE:-.worker-score.json}"

# Queue polling interval in seconds
POLL_INTERVAL="${POLL_INTERVAL:-5}"

# Exit when queue is empty (0 = run as perpetual daemon, 1 = run once and exit)
RUN_ONCE="${RUN_ONCE:-0}"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4.5 Workspace Isolation & Preview Staging
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Worker Isolation Mode:
#   1 = (Default) Dual-Worktree Isolation: Worker executes in .worker-tree
#       and publishes immutable preview snapshots to .preview/ on task PASS.
#       Enables safe early-access preview without collision.
#   0 = Single-Tree In-Place Mode: Worker executes directly in repository root.
#       Recommended for projects locked to fixed ports (e.g. port 22) or hardware.
WORKER_ISOLATION="${WORKER_ISOLATION:-1}"

# Enable terminal command sandbox (0 = disabled, 1 = enabled)
USE_SANDBOX="${USE_SANDBOX:-0}"

# Additional reference directories (comma-separated absolute paths)
# e.g., ADDITIONAL_DIRS="/Volumes/Vault500G/reference_project"
ADDITIONAL_DIRS="${ADDITIONAL_DIRS:-}"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Queue & Log File Paths (Relative to worker.sh directory)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TASKS_FILE="${TASKS_FILE:-tasks.txt}"
TASKS_DONE_FILE="${TASKS_DONE_FILE:-tasks.done}"
PROGRESS_FILE="${PROGRESS_FILE:-progress.log}"
PAUSE_FILE="${PAUSE_FILE:-PAUSE}"
